{"canonical_id":"stark:1529470","content":null,"evidence_id":"text:paper:1529470","overlay":{},"payload":{"abstract":"This paper presents both the theoretical (without solutions) and the experimental problems for the 42nd International Physics Olympiad (IPhO 42) organized in Bangkok, Thailand, 10–18 July 2012. Experimental problems on electrical and mechanical black boxes are given with detailed solutions. The performance of the contestants in the theoretical and the experimental sections is compared.","content":"Theoretical and experimental problems at IPhO 42 in Thailand

This paper presents both the theoretical (without solutions) and the experimental problems for the 42nd International Physics Olympiad (IPhO 42) organized in Bangkok, Thailand, 10–18 July 2012. Experimental problems on electrical and mechanical black boxes are given with detailed solutions. The performance of the contestants in the theoretical and the experimental sections is compared.","paper_id":1529470,"title":"Theoretical and experimental problems at IPhO 42 in Thailand"},"provenance":[{"dataset_version":"MMG-STaRK-MAG-v1","locator":"text/text_documents.parquet","schema_version":"1.0","source_id":"1529470"}],"source":"text"}
{"canonical_id":"stark:1534594","content":null,"evidence_id":"text:paper:1534594:overlay","overlay":{"origin":"phase4_evaluation_overlay","overlay_sha256":"ce96bbd1f2e6e1771c090b8c6c9f2db6b6d50f3a42a9aa9ce4f7dfa5877818da"},"payload":{"abstract":"We present an effective method of exact solution of the (1+1)-dimensional Dirac equation with a linear scalar-like potential in the context of the generalized uncertainty principle (GUP). The effectiveness of the method depends on knowledge of the energy spectrum of the harmonic oscillator with GUP. We employ the property of the harmonic oscillator that the kinetic energy part of the Hamiltonian is of equal weight to the potential energy part to obtain the energy levels from the deformation of the Dirac equation with a scalar-like linear potential through the generalized Heisenberg algebra of a GUP. Our result fully coincides with the results found in the literature. This paper thus provides an easier, alternative and effective method of exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential with GUP.","content":"Exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential under the influence of the generalized uncertainty principle

We present an effective method of exact solution of the (1+1)-dimensional Dirac equation with a linear scalar-like potential in the context of the generalized uncertainty principle (GUP). The effectiveness of the method depends on knowledge of the energy spectrum of the harmonic oscillator with GUP. We employ the property of the harmonic oscillator that the kinetic energy part of the Hamiltonian is of equal weight to the potential energy part to obtain the energy levels from the deformation of the Dirac equation with a scalar-like linear potential through the generalized Heisenberg algebra of a GUP. Our result fully coincides with the results found in the literature. This paper thus provides an easier, alternative and effective method of exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential with GUP.","evaluation_overlay":true,"paper_id":1534594,"title":"Exact solution of the Dirac equation with a linear potential under the influence of the generalized uncertainty principle"},"provenance":[{"dataset_version":"MMG-STaRK-MAG-v1","locator":"text/text_documents.parquet","schema_version":"1.0","source_id":"1534594"}],"source":"text"}
